1
00:00:00,867 --> 00:00:03,736
Now that we solved this ID problem,

2
00:00:04,494 --> 00:00:07,105
let's get back to HTMX and to

3
00:00:07,701 --> 00:00:10,103
features HTMX offers us.

4
00:00:11,587 --> 00:00:14,765
And one feature HTMX offers us, which I

5
00:00:14,878 --> 00:00:15,539
wanna use here,

6
00:00:16,176 --> 00:00:17,983
is a feature that allows me to

7
00:00:18,757 --> 00:00:21,920
make this code here a bit leaner.

8
00:00:22,737 --> 00:00:26,201
Because one problem I have with this code is

9
00:00:26,314 --> 00:00:29,783
that we're setting the target and hx-swap

10
00:00:30,104 --> 00:00:30,554
here

11
00:00:31,229 --> 00:00:31,662
in our

12
00:00:32,193 --> 00:00:34,619
root GET route when we render the entire

13
00:00:34,619 --> 00:00:34,956
page.

14
00:00:35,486 --> 00:00:37,640
And of course, I'm then repeating that same

15
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:40,383
code down there where I'm rendering that one

16
00:00:40,593 --> 00:00:42,078
single list item

17
00:00:42,659 --> 00:00:45,209
that is returned when we add a new goal.

18
00:00:46,932 --> 00:00:49,265
And we can actually get rid of this

19
00:00:49,265 --> 00:00:53,094
duplication of hx-swap at least by getting

20
00:00:53,190 --> 00:00:54,220
rid of it here

21
00:00:54,774 --> 00:00:58,062
And by also getting rid of it here in our

22
00:00:58,127 --> 00:00:59,185
main page content.

23
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:03,147
Now, of course, we need that hx-swap

24
00:01:03,147 --> 00:01:06,730
setting, but we can use an HTMX mechanism

25
00:01:06,746 --> 00:01:10,071
called inheritance for still applying it to

26
00:01:10,264 --> 00:01:11,459
all these list items.

27
00:01:12,946 --> 00:01:16,714
Because most HTMX attributes, not all of

28
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:20,207
them, but most of them can actually be set

29
00:01:20,207 --> 00:01:22,464
on a parent element and they will then

30
00:01:22,642 --> 00:01:23,941
automatically be inherited by all child

31
00:01:23,941 --> 00:01:24,185
elements.

32
00:01:27,565 --> 00:01:28,881
So we can add this

33
00:01:29,474 --> 00:01:32,956
hx-swap attribute to the unordered list,

34
00:01:33,325 --> 00:01:36,277
which will in the end hold all list items,

35
00:01:36,854 --> 00:01:39,325
no matter if they're rendered here as part

36
00:01:39,357 --> 00:01:42,293
of the overall page or if they're injected

37
00:01:42,405 --> 00:01:44,860
into the page later because a form was

38
00:01:44,988 --> 00:01:45,501
submitted.

39
00:01:46,657 --> 00:01:50,603
And we can set hx-swap to outerHTML here

40
00:01:50,748 --> 00:01:53,090
therefore, and all the list items and all

41
00:01:53,234 --> 00:01:55,769
the buttons in there will use that setting.

42
00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:59,238
Setting when they're using other HTMX

43
00:01:59,318 --> 00:02:01,454
attributes as we're doing it here, for

44
00:02:01,486 --> 00:02:02,049
example.

45
00:02:03,494 --> 00:02:06,818
And this inheritance concept is an important

46
00:02:07,027 --> 00:02:09,677
concept and you can always find out whether

47
00:02:09,677 --> 00:02:12,664
an attribute supports inheritance or not by

48
00:02:12,664 --> 00:02:15,604
taking a look at the documentation of that

49
00:02:15,716 --> 00:02:18,157
attribute. And if you then scroll down all

50
00:02:18,350 --> 00:02:20,309
the way to the bottom, you will find these

51
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:23,376
notes and there you learn that the element

52
00:02:23,488 --> 00:02:26,441
is inherited or whether it's not inherited.

53
00:02:27,822 --> 00:02:30,261
For example, all those attributes that

54
00:02:30,486 --> 00:02:33,342
trigger requests are not inherited,

55
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:36,247
which kind of makes sense because you don't

56
00:02:36,247 --> 00:02:38,558
wanna start sending the same kind of request

57
00:02:38,895 --> 00:02:41,880
for all the child elements of some element.

58
00:02:43,084 --> 00:02:46,550
hx-swap is inherited though, and therefore

59
00:02:46,695 --> 00:02:49,423
by setting it on the unordered list, instead

60
00:02:49,423 --> 00:02:52,228
of the buttons inside of the list, we can

61
00:02:52,228 --> 00:02:54,842
now make sure that if we reload

62
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:57,712
and we again add some items here,

63
00:02:58,321 --> 00:02:59,957
we got the same behavior as before.

64
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:03,292
The items are removed here, but we now made

65
00:03:03,292 --> 00:03:06,434
the code a bit leaner at least. And most

66
00:03:06,434 --> 00:03:08,583
importantly, you now know about this

67
00:03:08,583 --> 00:03:10,411
important inheritance concept.
